1
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:11,340
The caterer sent me this list of 12 appetizers. I have to narrow it to six.

2
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,670
Food? Oh, give me.

3
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:19,180
So did Monica tell you we're trying to get The Swing Kings to play the wedding?

4
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:21,020
Since when are you into swing music?

5
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,850
Since forever. I used to go all over town listening to bands.

6
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:28,400
Chandler.

7
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:28,400
Gap commercial.

8
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,860
So did you book them? Did you call?

9
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,860
I will.

10
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:38,370
You want me to call?

11
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:38,370
No. I'll do it. You stick to your job.

12
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,540
What is your job?

13
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,540
Staying out of the way.

14
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:46,580
This is impossible. Why don't you just pick all 15?

15
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:50,420
There were only 12.

16
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:50,420
Oh, yeah, I added three.

17
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:53,260
What are "peanut-butter fingers"?

18
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:45,640
Well, hello.

19
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:47,640
She's cute.

20
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:50,020
Should we go try to talk to her?

21
00:01:50,270 --> 00:01:55,440
Sure. The great thing about being engaged, I'm not nervous to talk to pretty girls anymore.

22
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:57,570
Could you guys help me?

23
00:02:00,570 --> 00:02:02,910
Yeah, let me get that for you.

24
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:06,950
It's really heavy.

25
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:06,950
I got it.

26
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:08,620
Oh!

27
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:14,800
So hi, I'm Ross, and this is my friend, Chandler.

28
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:18,760
I'm Kristen.

29
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:21,390
Kristen. Hi. Are you new to the area?

30
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,640
Because if you are, I'd love to show you around sometime.

31
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:28,350
I actually just moved from four blocks over.

32
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:28,350
Oh.

33
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:31,100
But this block is like a whole other world.

34
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:35,320
Actually, it does have a very interesting history.

35
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:40,990
This street is the first street in the city to have an underground sewer system.

36
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:44,320
Before that, sewage and waste...

37
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:47,790
...would just flow right down the street. Yeah.

38
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,660
Sometimes ankle-deep.

39
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:53,380
Smooth.

40
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:56,710
Excuse me?

41
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:05,010
You're gonna be starving after moving. What do you say I take you to dinner tonight?

42
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:06,970
I'd like that.

43
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:06,970
Yeah? Great.

44
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,430
Let me take this up.

45
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,940
After you.

46
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,940
Oh, no. After you.

47
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:15,480
Oh, my God!

48
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:26,740
Am I crazy, or does this totally go?

49
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:32,410
Oh, my God! You look so beautiful!

50
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:35,920
Thank you, Rachel. But look at Monica!

51
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,090
This is it. Yeah, this is the one.

52
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:42,590
I can't believe I found it.

53
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:47,470
Wow, you look so beautiful. If I knew you, I'd cry.

54
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:51,140
I'm Monica Geller. Ball like a baby.

55
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:52,730
I'm Megan Bailey.

56
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:56,610
Have you found your dress yet?

57
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:56,610
No. These dresses are all so amazing...

58
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:00,440
...but I couldn't afford one.

59
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:00,440
No, I can't afford this either.

60
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:05,530
I'm here to figure out the one I want, then I'll get it at Kleinman's, this discount place.

61
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:07,950
Day after tomorrow, they're having a huge sale.

62
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:11,500
Thanks for the tip.

63
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:11,500
When are you getting married?

64
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:16,790
I'm not. I just like to try these on.

65
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:16,790
I do the same thing.

66
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:21,510
I'm just kidding. I'm getting married July 25th.

67
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,550
I'm just kidding too. Ha, ha.

68
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,430
I'm getting married in December.

69
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,890
When are you getting married?

70
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,890
May 15th.

71
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:34,730
Ooh. It's close. So who's your photographer?

72
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,730
Jeffrey.

73
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,730
We met with him.

74
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:42,030
Did he show you nude wedding photos?

75
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:42,030
Best Man? Wow!

76
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:45,320
I know. I almost called off my wedding. Heh, heh, heh.

77
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:49,200
Oh, who's your band?

78
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:49,200
My fiancé wants The Swing Kings.

79
00:04:49,410 --> 00:04:53,540
You're lucky. My fiancé wants the heavy metal band, Carcass.

80
00:04:53,750 --> 00:04:58,670
Is that spelled with a "C" or a "K"? Oh, my God, it doesn't matter, they're both great!

81
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:02,500
Oh, you know what? Don't buy that here.

82
00:05:02,710 --> 00:05:06,340
Now that you know what you want, go to Kleinman's. Get it half off.

83
00:05:06,590 --> 00:05:08,720
This place is so over-priced.

84
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:10,850
I own this store.

85
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:16,020
So does this come in another color, or...

86
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:28,820
Hi. You moving in or moving out?

87
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:31,030
Moving in.

88
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:31,030
Can I give you a hand?

89
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:36,120
Okay, but be careful. The guy who was helping before had to leave because he hurt his back.

90
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,710
Boyfriend?

91
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,710
No.

92
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,630
I'm Joey.

93
00:05:41,290 --> 00:05:42,340
Kristen.

94
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:45,420
Wow. What a beautiful name.

95
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:48,340
What is it again?

96
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,760
Kristen.

97
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,760
Ah, that's it. Okay.

98
00:05:52,470 --> 00:05:55,220
You live around here?

99
00:05:52,470 --> 00:05:55,220
Yeah. Yeah, right down there.

100
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,310
Let me give you a tip.

101
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:02,310
Don't take a nap on this stoop. You could wake up without shoes.

102
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,820
I'll remember that.

103
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,820
Okay.

104
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:09,700
Listen, would you like to have dinner with me tonight?

105
00:06:09,910 --> 00:06:13,080
I have plans tonight. How about tomorrow?

106
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,870
Sounds great. Well, where does this go?

107
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,710
You look strong. I'll take that, you grab one of the boxes.

108
00:06:18,870 --> 00:06:20,920
Okay. Yeah.

109
00:06:24,670 --> 00:06:26,960
Yeah, I'll get this one.

110
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,760
What's taking so long?

111
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:36,010
Come on.

112
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:38,810
So this is Brooklyn?

113
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:43,110
All right, listen up. There's usually only one dress in each size.

114
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:46,780
So when they open those doors, fan out.

115
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:51,910
This is what you're looking for. Memorize it.

116
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:57,240
When you locate the dress blow on these, all right?

117
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:01,500
Three sharp blasts. When you hear it, come running.

118
00:07:01,670 --> 00:07:03,580
Okay, got it.

119
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,880
Here he comes!

120
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:08,300
Oh, they're pushing!

121
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:08,300
Don't be a baby!

122
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:11,010
Out of the way!

123
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:11,010
Let's go!

124
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:14,340
Hey, Rachel! Come on!

125
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:27,190
No. No, not it. Not it. Not it. Ugh.

126
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:31,990
Don't crowd me.

127
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:37,530
This is it! This is the dress! Oh, my God. It's perfect.

128
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:39,910
I'm sorry, this one's taken! Whoa!

129
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,870
Megan!

130
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,870
Monica!

131
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,750
You came!

132
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,750
Yeah!

133
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,710
This is my dress!

134
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,710
No!

135
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:52,880
Yes, it is. You saw me wearing it.

136
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:52,880
And now you'll see me buying it.

137
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:55,300
You freak!

138
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:58,310
You wouldn't even know about this place without me.

139
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:03,640
Look, you don't want to fight me.

140
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:03,640
Maybe I do. I'm pretty feisty!

141
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,770
I'm coming! I'm coming!

142
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,770
Hey!

143
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:10,110
Okay! Hey.

144
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:12,990
Oh, what do I do?!

145
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:23,500
What are you doing? Did you find the dress?

146
00:08:23,790 --> 00:08:25,170
Did you find the dress?

147
00:08:25,370 --> 00:08:28,170
No. You gotta get me out of here. These shoppers are crazy.

148
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,460
We've gotta get Monica.

149
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,460
You gotta hold my hand!

150
00:08:30,630 --> 00:08:31,800
Oh, my God.

151
00:08:33,170 --> 00:08:35,930
Excuse me! Excuse me!

152
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:40,180
Go! Go! Go!

153
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:42,140
Hey.

154
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:42,140
Go!

155
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,240
So, Ross, how was your date the other night?

156
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:59,490
Did you tell her about the magical ride that starts with the flush of every toilet?

157
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:05,870
Laugh all you want, but she left me a message saying she'd like to go out again.

158
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:09,420
Oh.

159
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:09,420
In fact, I'll go call her right now.

160
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:12,710
And I'll make sure and tell her my friend Chandler says...

161
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,550
Hey, Chandler.

162
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,550
Hey.

163
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:22,760
Sorry I didn't stop by last night, but I had a date.

164
00:09:22,970 --> 00:09:27,230
Joe, when it's 1:00 in the morning and you don't come by? That's okay.

165
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:32,320
Check it out. It was with this really hot girl who just moved in right across the street.

166
00:09:32,570 --> 00:09:35,320
Really? Right across the street?

167
00:09:32,570 --> 00:09:35,320
Yeah.

168
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:37,860
When did you meet her?

169
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:37,860
Two days ago.

170
00:09:38,070 --> 00:09:40,660
Excellent!

171
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:44,240
You know, Ross met somebody too.

172
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:44,240
Oh, yeah?

173
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:45,790
Hey.

174
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:45,790
How'd it go?

175
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:48,160
Great. We're going out again Saturday.

176
00:09:48,370 --> 00:09:53,170
But I found out she's also seeing some other guy.

177
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,920
Really?

178
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:02,300
Joe, what would you do if you were in Ross' situation?

179
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:06,810
Well, I sort of am. I'm dating this girl who's also seeing another guy.

180
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:09,190
But I'm not too worried about it.

181
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:14,650
You shouldn't be. Believe me, I wouldn't want to be the guy who's up against you.

182
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:19,150
I mean, that doofus is going to lose.

183
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:24,080
So this is nice.

184
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:29,790
I wish I didn't have to go. Believe me.

185
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,210
But I have to.

186
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:34,380
By the way, what's the name of the girl you're dating?

187
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:37,170
Kristen Leigh.

188
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:37,170
Bye.

189
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:48,600
Well, obviously, only one of us can keep dating her.

190
00:10:48,810 --> 00:10:52,480
Obviously. So how do we decide?

191
00:10:52,690 --> 00:10:56,190
Well now, let's look at this objectively.

192
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:58,740
I think I should date her.

193
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:02,030
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

194
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:05,740
Or I'm the one who dates her.

195
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:10,580
That's interesting. But check this out. I date her.

196
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,500
Yeah, I like that. But just to go in another direction...

197
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:16,130
Okay. This can go on for a while.

198
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,420
We should order some food then.

199
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,420
No, Joey.

200
00:11:20,970 --> 00:11:24,550
Look, why don't we just let her decide, okay?

201
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:27,600
We'll each go out with her one more time.

202
00:11:27,850 --> 00:11:30,430
And we'll see who she likes best.

203
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:33,810
That sounds fair.

204
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:37,860
Maybe I'll take her to that new French restaurant down the street.

205
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:41,530
Wait a second. We have to set a spending limit on the date.

206
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,570
I don't have the money to take her to a fancy place like that.

207
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:48,660
Well, sorry. That's what I do on dates.

208
00:11:48,870 --> 00:11:53,460
All right. Well, I guess I'll just have to do what I do on dates.

209
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:02,590
So let's decide on a spending limit.

210
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:02,590
Yeah.

211
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,470
Uh...

212
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:09,060
And a slice...

213
00:12:10,470 --> 00:12:12,430
Six dollars?

214
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:17,190
I was thinking more like a hundred.

215
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:17,190
Okay.

216
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:20,190
Can I borrow 94 dollars?

217
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,160
Uh.

218
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:30,540
I know. Can you hand me a tissue?

219
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:40,750
You're out of Diet Coke.

220
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:45,380
Hello?

221
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:49,550
What? You what?

222
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,600
You listen here, missy!

223
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:54,980
What?

224
00:12:55,190 --> 00:12:58,650
That was Megan. She booked The Swing Kings on the day of our wedding...

225
00:12:58,810 --> 00:13:01,400
...and said she'd only give them back for the dress!

226
00:13:03,110 --> 00:13:06,110
Does that mean Carcass is available?

227
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:12,240
What am I gonna do? That's the dress! That is "the" dress!

228
00:13:12,910 --> 00:13:16,290
Chandler wants the band. What do I do?

229
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:19,170
Figure out a way to talk him out of it.

230
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:19,170
How?

231
00:13:20,590 --> 00:13:22,750
You're out of toilet paper!

232
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:32,100
Hey.

233
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:32,100
What's up?

234
00:13:32,310 --> 00:13:35,230
I wanted to wish you good luck on your date.

235
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,690
Thanks.

236
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,690
What time are you meeting?

237
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:41,060
We have 8:00 reservations at Grand Merci Bistro.

238
00:13:41,270 --> 00:13:44,610
That's in 20 minutes. You'd better get dressed.

239
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:49,610
I am dressed.

240
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:49,610
Oh, well, good.

241
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:51,870
For me.

242
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:56,790
What's this? Did you give yourself a facial?

243
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,580
I have an oily T-zone.

244
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:02,710
Okay, dude.

245
00:14:05,710 --> 00:14:08,590
Hey, you sent Kristen flowers?

246
00:14:05,710 --> 00:14:08,590
That's right.

247
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:13,640
You spent 100 dollars. That's the limit. You're screwed!

248
00:14:14,470 --> 00:14:19,480
Actually, I sent the flowers before the actual date, so technically...

249
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:24,020
...technically, I didn't break any rules. Thanks for stopping by though.

250
00:14:24,230 --> 00:14:27,650
That's how it's gonna be? I can break the rules too.

251
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:30,410
What are you gonna do?

252
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:30,410
I don't know.

253
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,660
I'm not surprised.

254
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,660
You won't get away with this.

255
00:14:33,870 --> 00:14:35,540
You don't have much choice.

256
00:14:33,870 --> 00:14:35,540
We'll see!

257
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,040
Bye-bye.

258
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,040
Yeah, bye-bye.

259
00:14:39,710 --> 00:14:41,960
Hey! So just a light layer?

260
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:44,840
Yeah, just here and there.

261
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:55,050
Joey got meat sauce on the banister again.

262
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:58,270
Swing music is so out.

263
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:01,940
Phoebe, he's gotta be in the room for that to work.

264
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:05,320
What are you guys talking about?

265
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:08,030
We're talking about The Swing Kings...

266
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:10,990
...and whether they're the right way to go.

267
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,870
I went to a wedding where they had swing music...

268
00:15:14,030 --> 00:15:16,490
